---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqCategories = [
  {
    id: 'speaking',
    title: 'Speaking at an Event',
    icon: '🎤',
    subtitle: 'Call for Presentations (CFP), topics, mentorship, and our high-signal charter.',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'What topics are suitable for a Cyber Scotland Connect talk?',
        a: 'We welcome all topics focused on practical cyber security and defense: defensive engineering, threat intelligence, detection development, incident response, DevSecOps, cloud security, digital forensics, identity architecture, lessons learned from real incidents, and academic research. We also welcome career-transition reflections and community stories.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What is the "High-Signal, Zero-Sales" rule?',
        a: 'CSC gatherings are protected learning spaces, not marketing showcases. Speakers are permitted a brief 60-second intro about who they are and where they work, but the presentation itself must be 100% vendor-agnostic and educational. Product pitches, promotional demonstrations, and sales marketing are strictly prohibited.',
      },
      {
        q: 'I have never spoken at a tech meetup before. Can I submit?',
        a: 'Absolutely! We actively support and encourage first-time speakers, student researchers, and career-switchers. Our volunteer organizers offer optional 1-on-1 mentorship, draft slide reviews, and practice sessions to help you feel confident. Our room is notoriously friendly, constructive, and supportive.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What are the typical talk formats and lengths?',
        a: 'Our standard keynote slots are 25–35 minutes with 5–10 minutes of audience Q&A. We also frequently host 10–15 minute "Lightning Talks" which are ideal for short case studies, tool demonstrations, or first-time speakers.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How do I submit a talk proposal?',
        a: 'Simply send an email to organizers@cyberscotlandconnect.com with your name, a working title, a 2–3 sentence summary of what attendees will learn, and any AV requirements. You can also chat informally with any moderator on our Discord server.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'hosting',
    title: 'Hosting Us (Venues)',
    icon: '🏢',
    subtitle: 'Requirements, physical accessibility standards, and venue partnerships.',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'What does Cyber Scotland Connect look for in a host venue?',
        a: 'We look for welcoming spaces in central urban locations (close to train and bus stations) in Edinburgh, Glasgow, Dundee, and Aberdeen that can comfortably accommodate 60 to 100+ seated attendees with room for community mingling.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What physical accessibility standards are required?',
        a: 'Accessibility is mandatory for any CSC host venue: step-free access from the street, operational elevators to all event floors, accessible gender-neutral restrooms, and ideally induction hearing loop capabilities. We disclose accessibility baselines on every event listing.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What AV and technical equipment do you need?',
        a: 'A large presentation screen or projector with HDMI/USB-C connection, wireless handheld or lapel microphones, and reliable Wi-Fi for attendees. Having streaming or recording capabilities is a great bonus but not strictly required.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What recognition do host venues receive?',
        a: 'Host venues are featured prominently on our website Partners page, linked directly on our Meetup event notices, credited in slide openings, and announced during verbal opening remarks.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How can our company or university offer a venue?',
        a: 'Please reach out to partners@cyberscotlandconnect.com. A volunteer organizer will arrange a quick visit or call to review room layout and schedule future dates.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'sponsoring',
    title: 'Sponsoring Us (Ethical Sponsorship)',
    icon: '🤝',
    subtitle: 'Our transparent community funding model, attendee privacy, and social hosting.',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Where do community sponsorship funds go?',
        a: '100% of corporate sponsorship contributions go directly to attendee refreshments (community pizza, snacks, soft drinks), venue facility costs, recording equipment, and accessibility accommodations. CSC is a volunteer-led community; organizers take zero profit.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Can a sponsor buy a speaking slot?',
        a: 'No. Zero exceptions. Speaking slots are never sold or tied to financial sponsorships. Every presentation abstract is evaluated purely on its educational and technical merit by our volunteer team.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Do sponsors receive attendee contact information or email lists?',
        a: 'Never. Attendee privacy is non-negotiable. We never disclose, sell, or share attendee emails, phone numbers, or registration data with sponsors. Sponsors are welcome to engage in open, transparent conversation with attendees during mingling time.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Can our company sponsor a post-event social or networking drinks?',
        a: 'Yes! Sponsoring our post-meetup pub social (such as Cyera UK hosting our community social at BrewDog Lothian Road) is a popular and appreciated way to support informal Scottish cyber networking.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How can our organization discuss sponsorship packages?',
        a: 'Contact partners@cyberscotlandconnect.com to explore upcoming gathering dates across Edinburgh, Glasgow, and Dundee.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'community',
    title: 'Community Basics & Pay It Forward',
    icon: '☕',
    subtitle: 'Free tickets, Pay It Forward coffee donations, and our community pledge.',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Are Cyber Scotland Connect events really free?',
        a: 'Yes! Tickets have always been, and will always be, £0. We believe financial barriers to entry should never prevent anyone—especially students, career switchers, and job seekers—from participating in Scottish cyber security.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What is the "Pay It Forward" Buy Me a Coffee initiative?',
        a: 'For established professionals who attend our sessions and find value in the network, we invite you to Pay It Forward on our Buy Me a Coffee page (buymeacoffee.com/cyberscotlandconnect). There is zero obligation; contributions help fund refreshments and ensure everyone in Scotland can attend at no cost.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What is the Cyber Scotland Connect Code of Conduct?',
        a: 'We adhere to the Contributor Covenant v2.1. We enforce a zero-tolerance policy regarding harassment, exclusionary language, and unwelcome sales prospecting. All participants, speakers, and organizers must uphold these standards.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How do I stay connected between meetups?',
        a: 'Join our active Discord server (discord.gg/cyberscotlandconnect), follow our LinkedIn organization page, and RSVP via our Meetup group (meetup.com/cyberscotconnect).',
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="FAQ & Get Involved" 
  description="Everything you need to know about speaking at Cyber Scotland Connect, hosting a gathering, ethical sponsorship, and community guidelines."
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-[#3e3c66] pb-8 mb-12 transition-colors">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#56548c] dark:text-[#6fb7e6] block mb-1">
        Community Knowledgebase
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-tight transition-colors">
        FAQ & Getting Involved
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-[#bdaccf] text-base mt-2 max-w-3xl transition-colors">
        Clear guidance for speakers submitting talks, tech hubs offering venues, organizations exploring ethical sponsorship, and attendees joining our grassroots community.
      </p>

      <!-- Jump Links Bar -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-8" aria-label="FAQ Category Navigation">
        {faqCategories.map(cat => (
          <a
            href={`#${cat.id}`}
            class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold bg-slate-100 dark:bg-[#2a2948] text-slate-700 dark:text-[#bdaccf] hover:bg-[#895294] hover:text-white dark:hover:bg-[#895294] border border-slate-200 dark:border-[#3e3c66] transition-all flex items-center gap-1.5"
          >
            <span>{cat.icon}</span>
            <span>{cat.title}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Sections -->
    <div class="space-y-16">
      {faqCategories.map(category => (
        <section id={category.id} class="scroll-mt-24">
          <!-- Category Header -->
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5 mb-6 pb-4 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-[#3e3c66]">
            <span class="text-3xl p-2 rounded-xl bg-purple-50 dark:bg-[#382b5c] border border-purple-200 dark:border-[#56548c] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">
              {category.icon}
            </span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wide">
                {category.title}
              </h2>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-[#bdaccf] mt-0.5">
                {category.subtitle}
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Questions Accordion / Cards List -->
          <div class="space-y-4">
            {category.items.map((item, idx) => (
              <details class="group bg-white dark:bg-[#2a2948] rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-[#3e3c66] shadow-sm overflow-hidden transition-all duration-200 open:border-[#895294] dark:open:border-[#6fb7e6]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer select-none text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white group-hover:text-[#895294] dark:group-hover:text-[#6fb7e6] transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#6fb7e6]">
                  <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 dark:text-slate-500">0{idx + 1}</span>
                    <span>{item.q}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="ml-4 shrink-0 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
                    ▼
                  </span>
                </summary>
                <div class="px-5 sm:px-6 pb-6 pt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-[#bdaccf] leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-[#3e3c66]/40">
                  <p>{item.a}</p>
                </div>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Bottom Contact & Action Box -->
    <div class="mt-20 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-[#1b1a30] rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-[#3e3c66] p-8 sm:p-12 text-center transition-colors">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase mb-3">
        Still Have Questions?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-[#bdaccf] text-sm max-w-lg mx-auto mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        Our volunteer leadership team is always happy to discuss presentation proposals, venue bookings, accessibility requirements, and ethical partnerships.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="mailto:organizers@cyberscotlandconnect.com"
          class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-[#895294] hover:bg-[#9d5fa8] text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-md transition-all flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <span>Email Organizers</span> ✉️
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://discord.gg/cyberscotlandconnect"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-[#2a2948] hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-[#382b5c] border border-slate-300 dark:border-[#56548c] text-slate-800 dark:text-white font-semibold text-sm transition-all shadow-sm flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <span>Ask in Discord</span> ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
